  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "For any vector $\\mathbf{x},$ where $\\hat{\\mathbf{i}}, \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}, \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}$ have their usual meanings the value of $(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{i}})^{2}+(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{j})^{2}+(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{k})^{2}$ where $\\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j}, \\mathbf{k}$ have their usual meanings, is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3Cwva",
      "text": "$|\\mathbf{x}|^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "P6b55",
      "text": "$2|\\mathbf{x}|^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "m77Me",
      "text": "$3|\\mathbf{x}|^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "v6gjv",
      "text": "$4|\\mathbf{x}|^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathbf{x}=\\alpha \\mathbf{i}+\\beta \\mathbf{j}+\\gamma \\mathbf{k}$\r\nThen, $\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{i}=-\\beta \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}+\\gamma \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\mathbf{x} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{j}} &=\\hat{\\mathbf{k}}-\\gamma \\hat{\\mathbf{i}} \\\\ \\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{k} &=-\\alpha \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}+\\beta \\hat{\\mathbf{i}} \\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\text {Now, }(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{i})^{2} &=(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{i}) \\cdot(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{i}}) \\\\ &=(-\\beta \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}+\\gamma \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}) \\cdot(-\\beta \\hat{\\mathbf{k}}+\\gamma \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}) \\\\ &=\\beta^{2}+\\gamma^{2} \\end{aligned}$\r\nSimilarly, $(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{j})^{2}=\\alpha^{2}+\\gamma^{2}$\r\nand $(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{k})^{2}=\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}$\r\n$\\therefore(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{i})^{2}+(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{j})^{2}+(\\mathbf{x} \\times \\mathbf{\\mathbf { k }})^{2}$\r\n$=\\beta^{2}+\\gamma^{2}+\\alpha^{2}+\\gamma^{2}+\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}$\r\n$=2\\left(\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}+\\gamma^{2}\\right)=2|\\mathbf{x}|^{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
